    tags: ["test center", "quizzes", "questions", "topics"],
    content: "# How content is organised\n\n**Program → Quiz → Topic → Question.** For example: Cybersecurity Bootcamp → Introduction to Cybersecurity → Networking basics → individual questions.\n\n> **Quiz, not course.** What the Test Center used to call a \"course\" is a **quiz**: a bank of practice questions grouped into topics. The word **course** is now reserved for learning courses (lessons and enrolments), which are a separate feature. Some screens still say \"course\" while the wording is being updated.\n\n# Who does what\n\n- **Staff:** open the Test Center with the **gear** on the dashboard card. Write questions and submit them for review.\n- **Managers and above:** create programs, quizzes and topics, review and publish questions, and import question files.\n- **Members:** see only **published** questions, in the learner view.\n\n# Writing a question\n\n1. Open the topic and choose to add a question.\n2. Choose **multiple choice** (at least two options) or **true/false**.\n3. Mark the correct answer and add an **explanation** (shown after answering) and an optional **hint**.\n4. Set the **difficulty** (easy, medium, hard) and tags.\n5. Submit for review, or publish if you are a manager.\n\n# Program counts\n\nEach program shows how many quizzes it contains. A program that still has quizzes cannot be deleted.\n\n> Many questions at once? Use **Import** (see \"Importing Test Center questions from CSV or JSON\").",
