    content: "# Who\n\nManagers, admins and owners. Open the Test Center (gear) → **Import** (or **Import Questions** in the menu).\n\n# Steps\n\n1. **Choose a file:** CSV (Excel: Save As → **CSV UTF-8**; or Google Sheets download) or JSON. Up to 2,000 questions and 5 MB.\n2. **Defaults:** pick the course, program for new courses, topic (default \"General\") and status (Published or Draft) for rows that leave them blank.\n3. **Review:** see how many programs, courses, topics and questions are new or will be updated, duplicates in the file, and every skipped row with its line number and reason. Nothing is saved yet.\n4. **Import:** a progress bar shows the work. Missing programs, courses and topics are created first.\n\n# CSV columns\n\n- **program, course, topic:** names; matched to existing ones ignoring case and punctuation.\n- **question:** required.\n- **type:** multiple-choice (default) or true-false.\n- **option_a … option_f:** at least two for multiple choice.\n- **correct_answer:** the option letter or exact option text; true/false for true-false questions.\n- **explanation, hint:** optional.\n- **difficulty:** easy, medium (default) or hard; beginner/advanced are accepted.\n- **tags:** separated by ; , or |\n- **id:** optional stable key. With an id, re-importing **updates** instead of duplicating.\n\nWithout an id, a re-import matches a question by its text within the same topic. Commas, semicolons and tabs are detected automatically.\n\n> Rows skipped? Each one shows the reason. Fix the file and import again; rows already imported are updated, not duplicated.",
