    slug: "community-overview",
    title: "Zebron Community and your organization's community",
    summary: "The difference between the public Zebron Community and private organization communities, and what you can do in each.",
    applicationKey: "community",
    contentType: "guide",
    category: "Community",
    audience: ["all"],
    tags: ["community", "posts", "privacy"],
    content: "# Two communities\n\n- **Public Zebron Community** (/community): everyone signed in can read and post.\n- **Organization community** (from your partner dashboard): only **active members of that organization** can see it. Posts never appear in the public feed.\n\nPosts are created in the community you are viewing, so check which one you are in before posting.\n\n# What everyone can do\n\n- Post, comment, react, save posts and **report** a post.\n- **Edit or delete your own posts** and delete your own comments.\n- Start a chat with another person; only the two of you can read it or its attachments (up to 50 MB).\n\n# Moderators\n\n- **Public community:** Zebron platform administrators.\n- **Organization community:** managers, admins and owners of that organization.\n\nModerators can hide, restore or remove posts and remove comments. Topics are managed by the same people.\n\n> Deleting is \"soft\": a deleted comment is blanked but replies to it stay visible.",
