    audience: ["support"],
    tags: ["support queue", "partner requests", "operations"],
    content: "# Support queue (Admin → Support)\n\n1. Work **Needs a reply** and **Unassigned** first; urgent tickets sort to the top.\n2. Assign to yourself, reply, and use **internal notes** for private context.\n3. Set **Resolved** when done. Resolved tickets close after 7 days; a reply reopens them.\n\n# Partner requests (Admin → Partner Requests)\n\n- Approve buttons say what will happen: provision, suspend, retire, transfer ownership.\n- Reject with a note. Terminations are acknowledged, not rejected.\n- **Partner agreement** tab: edit and save a new version; owners are asked to accept it.\n\n# Other daily checks\n\n- **Contact Mailbox:** platform inbound email and request notifications (see \"Working the Zebron contact mailbox\").\n- **Community moderation:** Admin → Community → Moderation for the public community's reports.\n- **Knowledge Center:** keep Zebron articles current; partners see them by audience and by the applications they have.\n- **Organizations:** review new applications and move them through review, approval and provisioning.\n- **Blog:** the admin dashboard's **Blog** tool opens Review & manage for the public blog; **Internal Blog** opens the staff-only section (see \"Reading and writing on the Zebron blog\").\n\n# Weekly\n\n- Firebase console → Functions → Logs for errors.\n- App Check metrics (while it isn't enforced yet) and budget alerts.",
